Deep Dive to AWS EBS CSI Driver in EKS ☁️

◾Since the AWS EBS CSI Driver runs inside the EKS cluster, it needs permission to create and manage storage in AWS.

◾The IAM Policy defines what the driver is allowed to do:
  - ec2:CreateVolume
  - ec2:AttachVolume
  - ec2:DetachVolume
  - ec2:DeleteVolume
  - ec2:CreateSnapshot
  - ec2:DescribeVolumes

◾The policy alone is not enough.
◾It must be attached to an IAM Role.
◾Role the CSI Driver  assumes to get AWS access.
◾In EKS, this is  done with IRSA.
◾The CSI Driver runs with a Kubernetes ServiceAccount.
That ServiceAccount is trusted by the IAM Role.
◾When the CSI Driver needs to call AWS, it assumes that role and receives temporary AWS credentials.
